 ],
 "coverageNotes": [
  "Executive Council and county commissioner district boundary lines aren't on our map yet. Those contests are listed here because the Secretary of State's own district assignments place Newbury in Executive Council District 2 and the county's Second Commissioner District — the town assignment is sourced even though the lines can't be drawn.",
  "Candidates can also reach the November ballot by nomination papers (the route independents and smaller parties use). The Secretary of State certifies those filings by September 2, 2026, so they can't be listed yet — the lists here show everyone who filed for the party primaries.",
  "Why no question: putting a constitutional amendment (CACR) on the ballot takes a three-fifths vote of both chambers, and every CACR proposed in the 2025-2026 General Court fell short or was killed — CACR 6 (right to compute), 12 (tax supermajority), 14 (citizenship for office), 15 (hunt and fish), 21 (voting eligibility), 24 (parental privacy in education), and 28 (public protestant teachers). Vote records verified against legislative-tracking services 2026-08-14. CORRECTED 2026-08-21 under RULING 52: this note used to end 'the General Court's own site (gc.nh.gov) refuses every client this project has, browsers included — recorded in the source ladder.' That was true when it was written on 2026-08-14 and is FALSE now — re-walked 2026-08-21, gc.nh.gov answers a plain rung-2 fetch at HTTP 200. A wall is recorded with the date it was last tested, never as a standing property, and this sentence went unchecked for a week because it read as a fact rather than as a measurement. The CACR vote records above are unaffected and stand as verified."
 ]
}
